        "object": "<p>Head of National Cyber Security Centre says UK in ‘ongoing contest with capable adversaries’ and AI could add to threat </p><p>The UK’s critical national infrastructure has been hit by more than 200 cyber incidents over the past year and state-linked assailants were behind three-quarters of the attacks, according to the state cybersecurity body.</p><p>Richard Horne, the chief executive of the National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC), said hostile states such as Russia, China and Iran were increasingly targeting systems behind the UK’s key services.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/jun/17/uk-critical-infrastructure-cyber-incidents-ncsc\">Continue reading...</a>"
